* PD5: a PROBE traces one wavelength of a multi-wavelength net in a .tran; MLPROBEs give the reference.
* m carries 1550 nm (cwsrc2) and 1560 nm (cwsrc1) from the operating point; m2 also gets 1540 nm from
* vlsrc1 at 2 ps; c only carries 1540 nm (no operating-point value).
*   probe1 (m): 1550 nm, the smallest wavelength at the enable (operating-point values), = mlprobe2@1550
*   probe3 (m2): 1550 nm; the 1540 nm light, smaller but arriving later, is ignored, = mlprobe3@1550
*   probe4 (c): 1540 nm, latched in the first time step that brings any, = mlprobe4@1540
*   probe5 (c, wl=0): wl=0 is ignored since PD6: it traces its wavelength, as probe4
* stderr: the PD6 warning for wl=0 (at elaboration), one warning per probe that ignores a wavelength, one line for the automatic probes (traceall).
cwsrc1 a wl=1.56e-6 power=1e-3
cwsrc2 b wl=1.55e-6 power=4e-3
merger1 a b m
vlsrc1 c values=[[2e-12, 2e-3, 1.54e-6], [6e-12, 0, 1.54e-6]]
merger2 m c m2
probe1 m
probe3 m2
probe4 c
probe5 c wl=0
mlprobe2 m wl=[1.55e-6, 1.56e-6]
mlprobe3 m2 wl=[1.54e-6, 1.55e-6, 1.56e-6]
mlprobe4 c wl=[1.54e-6]
.options traceall=1
.tran 10e-12
